<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One page of verse, set in one block. Page number top right. Signature at foot.</layout>
  <page_number>187</page_number>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>Aa 4</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Sed qui supremi Numinis aureas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Leges seruetur, quæ vetitum nefas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Fraudesque damnat: cui bene conscia</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Et pura mens est, quique humili prece</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Cœlo potentem sollicitat Patrem,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Speratque sera præmia gloria</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Christi recumbens pollicitis, truces</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Mylí, paludes Tartareas Stygis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Et damna prædo quæ parat impiger,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Ridet, necacrem pauperiem timet</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Contentus arcto siuere sub lare,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Et pane sesci, quem Deus in diem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Largitur alma munificus manu.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Quid? Rege Lydo ditior occupat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Nomen beati, compede quem fera</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Victor ligatum Persa suos sequi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Nutus coegit iussaque turpia.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Quid? Ille magnis pauperiem haud suam</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Mutare Crassi diuitiis volet,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Parthus recisum cui liquido caput</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Immerfit auro: quaque sitiuerant</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Explere fuluis compulit improbas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Fauces metallis. Copia diuites</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Non nutrit aris, plena nec horrea</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Febres repellunt corpore languido.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Immensa pascit dextera Cœlitum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Blandas volucres, dum Boreas furit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Et rura diro cuncta rigent gelu,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29">
      <i>Quid, quaeso, votis supplicium abnuet!</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Several words are uncertain in the scan: "seruetur" and "setitum" (the first letters are hard to make out), "Myli" [?] and "sesci" [?] could be misread; the long s has been rendered as plain s. The line "Quid, quaeso" is read from the underlined word and may be doubtful.</notes>
</page>
